  why: 'SCDES predicts king tides Oct 26 to 29 and Nov 24 to 27, the last on its 2026 list. WMBF Oct 7, 2025 (updated Oct 10) gives the 7 ft minor level, the 8.6 ft forecast peak of a storm-boosted tide, and the streets it expected to flood in that one event. NOAA 8661070 hilo predictions: Oct 27 8:36 AM 6.87 ft and Oct 28 9:24 AM 6.85 ft are the two highest of 2026; evening highs run 1.0 to 1.5 ft lower; Oct 30 11:18 AM 6.42 ft; Thanksgiving 8:11 AM 6.80 ft; Nov 28 10:04 AM 6.27 ft; Dec 24 7:06 AM 6.55 ft and Dec 25 7:59 AM 6.53 ft. NOAA lists the NWS minor level at Springmaid as 7.0 ft MLLW (moderate 8.5). Live Monday Oct 26 about 7 AM EDT, close to the first king tide, so the prep points at Tuesday morning.',
